That's not always preferred, though. Sometimes you like to see the
clock while you're playing Nethack.  A better solution is to SET the
font used for the windowed console to something you like.

After you've started tty Nethack in Windows, right-click the title bar
and choose Properties from the context menu. Go to the Font tab and
choose a nice font. You can use any monospaced truetype font[*] on your
system, or choose from a selection of fixed system fonts, listed by the
number of pixels they occupy: 5x12, 8x8, etc. A "window preview"
conveniently shows you how big the window will be on your desktop.

You can also go to the Layout tab and set the number of rows to
something huge -- the extra rows won't be used by the Nethack level
map, but they will be used when you look at long inventory listings or
help menus.

Finally, click OK. You'll be asked if you want to (a) apply properties
to this window only, or (b) modify the shortcut that started the
window, or (c) perhaps save the properties for windows with the same
title. Choose (b) or (c), whichever is shown - that way Nethack will
always use those properties. Click OK once more and you're in business!



